311, 1, 445, 26,
818, 2, 878, 52, 2
Food
This shows the amount of food stored in your Kingdom.  The numbers in parenthesis show the positive or negative change in this amount over the past year.
~
311, 1, 445, 26,
818, 2, 878, 52, 1
Food
This shows the amount of food that you have in reserve.  This food is only for free human units that you control.
~
311, 27, 445, 51,
891, 2, 960, 52, 0
Treasure
This shows the amount of money in your treasury.  Get more money by trade, tax or looting. The numbers in parenthesis show the positive or negative change in this amount over the past year.
~
460, 6, 558, 22,
864, 57, 957, 71, 0
Date
This shows current date.
~
487, 23, 550, 53,
971, 2, 1018, 52, 2
Reputation
This shows your Kingdom's reputation.
~
487, 23, 550, 53,
971, 2, 1018, 52, 1
Life Points
This shows the number of Life Points that you have in reserve.
Get more life points by killing living beings.
~
720, 8, 743, 31,
944, 176, 967, 199, 0
Terrain Map
This map shows the world's natural features & the location of towns, resources & units.
~
744, 32, 767, 55,
968, 200, 991, 223, 0
World Political Map
This map shows all the world's towns, buildings, units & resources.
~
768, 56, 791, 79,
992, 224, 1015, 247, 0
Trade Map
This map mode shows the location of markets, mines, factories, towns and caravans.
~
619, 16, 647, 44,
843, 184, 870, 211, 0
Hide Buildings
Clicking here will hide all structures other than towns.
You will instead see color coded squares with the names of the buildings.
~
NATION
Nationality
This button shows all possessions belonging to the same player as the selected unit or building.  Right-Click here to lock this button.  If you then select another unit of a different color, the small world map will not change.
~
OBJECT
Object
This button shows all object of the same type as the selected object.  Right-Click here to lock this button.
If you then select another object, the small world map will not change.
~
BRIBE
Bribe
This will take you to a menu where you can choose a bribe amount to offer to the selected person.
You will be unable to bribe if your spy does not have the necessary skill.
~
BUILD
Build (ALT-B)
Click here to select a structure to build.
You will not be able to build those structures listed on the darkened buttons until you have done the appropriate research or until you have enough money.
~
CANCEL
Cancel
This will cancel your present action.
~
CAPTURE
Capture
This will capture the selected structure.
This action may result in war.
~
CHGPROD
Change Production
This will toggle production in this factory between iron, copper and clay products.
Make sure that your production matches your raw materials.
~
CHG-TASK
Change Task
Clicking here will toggle the tasks performed in this structure.
~
CHG-MISS
Change Spy's Mission
Clicking here will toggle the mission assigned to the selected spy.
~
COLLTAX
Collect Tax (ALT-T)
This will collect tax from the selected town.
If you right-click on this icon you will be able to choose an auto-tax for your citizens.
~
CONTINUE
Continue
~
DEFENSE0
At Ease (click or ALT-A to switch mode)
This orders your troops to remain in the fort even when it is attacked.
~
F_DEFEN0
At Ease (click or ALT-A to switch mode)
This orders your troops to remain in the lair even when it or linked slave towns are attacked.
~
DEFENSE1
Alert! (click or ALT-A to switch mode)
This orders your troops to sortie whenever the fort or linked structures are attacked.
~
F_DEFEN1
Alert! (click or ALT-A to switch mode)
This orders your troops to sortie whenever the lair or a linked slave town is attacked.
~
ARM_TOWERS
Arm Towers
Click here to arm from 1 to 5 of your fort's towers.
If your towers are armed, they will fire on the enemy when your fort is attacked.
~
TOWERS
Towers
These icons show how many of your fort's towers are armed.
Red color on a tower shows that it is in the process of being armed.
~
DEMOTE
Demote Unit
This will demote the selected General to a common soldier.
Demotion will cause the unit's loyalty to fall.
~
F_DEMOTE
Demote Unit
This will demote the selected Ordo to a common croul.
Demotion will cause the unit's loyalty to fall.
~
F_GRANT
Payoff
Click here to see how much money it will take to purchase the loyalty of this independent lair.
~
GRANT
Grant (ALT-G)
This will grant money to the selected town.
If you right-click on this you will be able to grant money automatically to your towns when their loyalty reaches a certain level.
~
GRANT2
Grant
This will grant money to the selected town, thus lowering the town's resistance to your rule.
~
HIRECARA
Hire Caravan (ALT-C)
This will hire a caravan from this market so that you can conduct trade.
It will be disabled if you have too few citizens to support any more caravans.
10 citizens are needed to support each caravan.
~
CARACOPY
Clone Caravan
This will hire a new caravan that copies the trading route and cargo of the selected caravan. 
~
ITEMICON
Purchase Artifact
Click on this Artifact to purchase it. When you do, it will be seen on the ground outside of the inn.
~
HIREUNIT
Hire Person (ALT-H)
Clicking on this icon will hire the selected mercenary.
~
F_ANIMAL
Hire an animal
Clicking here will hire the selected animal.
~
MAKESHIP
Build a Ship
This takes you to a menu where you can select ships to build in this harbor.
~
MAKEWEAP
Make a Weapon (ALT-W)
This takes you to a menu where you can select the type and number of weapons that you want to produce.
~
MAKEWEA2
Make a Mega Weapon (ALT-M)
This takes you to a menu where you can select the type and number of mega 	weapons that you want to produce.
~
MOBILSPY
Mobilize Spy
This will send the selected spy out of the place where he has been infiltrated.
~
MOBILIZE
Mobilize Unit
This will send the selected unit out of the place.
~
OUTSHIP
Disembark from Ship
The will disembark all of the units from this ship.
This tile will be disabled if your ship is not close enough to the shore.
~
PATROL
Sortie (ALT-S)
This will sortie all of the fully trained troops from this Fort.  Right-Click on a soldier if you want to remove only him.
If you Right-Click on this icon you can choose two other options:  Sortie No Leader and Sortie No Injured.
~
F_PATROL
Sortie (ALT-S)
This will sortie all of the fully trained troops from this lair. Right-Click on a croul if you want to remove only him.
If you Right-Click on this icon you can choose two other options:  Sortie No Leader and Sortie No Injured.
~
RETCAMP
Withdraw (ALT-W)
This will immediately withdraw your soldier or the entire troop to its home fort or camp.
Right click here to choose the health level at which the selected unit will be withdrawn to his home fort.
~
F_RETCMP
Withdraw (ALT-W)
This will immediately withdraw your unit or the entire troop to its home lair.
Right click here to choose the health level at which the selected unit will be withdrawn to his home lair.
~
PREVMENU
Previous Menu
This will return you to the previous menu.
~
PROMOTE
Promote (ALT-R)
This will promote the selected common soldier to General.
~
F_PROMOT
Promote (ALT-R)
This will promote the selected croul to Ordo.
~
RECRUIT
Recruit (ALT-R)
This will recruit a civilian from the selected town.
For each click, one civilian will exit. This tile will be disabled if
there are no more civilians in the town.
~
WAGON
Wagon transport
Clicking on this icon will hire a wagon carrying a maximum of 10 civilians. 
You may send the wagon into another town or use it to build a new town.
If you find that the wagon cannot enter a town, it may be because the town has too many people or is of a different nationality.
~
RESEARCH
Conduct Research (ALT-R)
Clicking on this icon will give you a choice of areas of research for your Towers of Science.
After you choose an area, you must then choose a specific topic.
Choosing for one Tower of Science will set the same research project for all.
~
F_RESE
Buy Knowledge
Clicking on this icon will give you a choice of  knowledge that you can buy.
Subjects on the white buttons will be available to you.  If no buttons are white it means that you cannot afford to buy any knowledge.
~
REWARD
Honors (ALT-H)
This will award an honor to the selected unit.
For each honor, the person's loyalty will increase by 10 points.
This icon will be disabled for the King, whose loyalty is always the maximum..
~
F_REWARD
Honors (ALT-H)
This will award an honor to the selected Fryhtan.
For each honor, the Fryhtan's loyalty will increase by 10 points.
This icon will be disabled for the All High, whose loyalty is always the maximum.
~
SELBRIBE
Offer Bribe
Click on this icon to choose the amount of bribe money to offer to the selected unit.
~
SETTLE
Build a Town
This orders the selected unit to build a town in which he will settle.
Selecting more than one unit will not increase the speed of construction.
~
SPYMENU
Spy Menu
Go to the spy menu.
~
SPYCAPT
Capture Enemy Structure
Clicking here will capture the enemy structure.
This action may result in war.
~
SPYCHACT
Spy's Task
This orders your spy to change his task.
~
SPYNOTI0
Notification is currently disabled. Click to enable.
While disabled, your spy's change of color a will remain secret.
You will retain the ability to control your spy's movement.
~
SPYNOTI1
Notification is currently enabled. Click to disable.
While enabled, your spy's change of color will be announced to the Kingdom that he is joining.
You will lose your ability to control your spy's movement.
~
SUCCEED
Succeed to the Crown
This will elevate the selected person to the Crown.
You may elevate anyone, but those with high leadership skills will be the best.
~
TRAIN
Train (ALT-T)
Clicking on this icon will take one civilian from the town with green sphere recruit link and put him into the fort where he will begin his military training.
This icon will be disabled if there are no more civilians in the town or if the fort is full.
~
S_TRAIN
Train Special Unit (ALT-T)
Clicking on this icon will take one civilian from the town and put him into this building where he will begin his military training.
This icon will be disabled if there are no more civilians in the town or if the building is full.
~
F_TRAIN
Breed (ALT-B)
Clicking on this icon will start the breeding of a new Fryhtan.
This icon will be disabled if the lair is full or if you do not have enough Life Points.
~
TRAIN-C
Train Civilian Spy
Click here to take a civilian from the town and begin his training as a civilian spy.
~
TRAIN-I
Train Infantry Spy
Click here to take a civilian from the town and begin his training as an infantry spy.
~
TRAIN-S
Train Special Unit Spy
Click here to take a civilian from the town and begin his training as a special unit spy.
~ 
VSECRET
Steal Secrets
This will take you to a menu where you can select secrets to steal.
The skill level of your spy will determine the levels of secrets that will be available for theft.
~
NOSPY
Drop spy identity
This will cause the spy to give up his life of espionage.
~
AUTOPICK
Automatic
With this set your caravans will automatically pick up the surplus goods from this market.
~
NOPICK
Nothing
With this set your caravans will not pick up anything from this market.
~
RESIGN
Disband a unit
This will disband the selected unit. If the selected unit is a foreign spy, this will execute him.
~
CSETSTOP
Select a new trade stop.
After clicking this button, click on the location where you want your caravan to stop.
~
CGOSTOP
View a caravan's trade stop
This will center your screen over this caravan stop.
~
CDELSTOP
Delete a trade stop.
Clicking here will delete this trade stop for the selected caravan.
~
CCLRSEL
Clear selections.
Clicking here will clear the settings for your caravan's loading.
After clearing, select the goods that you want your caravan to carry. 
~
SSETSTOP
Set a ship's trade stop
After you press this button, click your cursor on the harbor where you want your trading ship to stop.
~
SGOSTOP
View a ship's trade stop
This will center your screen over this ship's trading stop.
~
SDELSTOP
Delete a ship's trade stop
Clicking here will delete this ship's trade stop.
~
DESTFIRM
Demolish this building
Clicking here will demolish this structure.
~
SELLFIRM
Sell this building
Clicking here will sell this structure, although you will get less than it cost to build.
~
REPAIR
Repair this building. Right click to repair All. 
Click on this icon to begin repairing this structure.
Click again to stop and restart.
Right-Click on this icon to automatically repair all of your buildings.
~
REPAIRING
Building under repair
Click here to stop the repair of this building.
Click again to restart.
~
REPLYDIP
Reply to diplomatic message
Click on this colored box to reply to this diplomatic message.
Right-Click to "Accept".
~
GOTO
Go to this event
Click on this icon to center your screen over this event.
~
NEWSLOG
News Log (hotkey: F9)
Click on this to bring up the news report log.
~
CLRNEWS
Clear news messages (hotkey: X)
Click on this to clear all news messages on the screen. You may also press X on your keyboard.
~
GAMEMENU
Game Menu (hotkey: F10)
Click here to bring up the Game Menu.
~
MK_STOCK
Stock
This shows the current stock of this type of goods in the market.
Make sure that your markets are linked to your factories so that they can most easily receive goods.
~
MK_SALES
Sales
This shows the total sales of this type of goods in the market in the past 365 days.
Make trade agreements with other Kingdoms to increase your sales, or export your excess goods to your other markets.
~
MK_DEMAN
Demand
This shows the monthly demand for goods from towns linked to this market.
~
MK_INCOM
Yearly Income
This shows the total income of this market in the past 365 days.
~
MK_CLEAR
Clear Stock
Click on this button to clear all of the stock of this type of goods in the market.
~
FC_PROD
Monthly Production
This shows the quantity of the product manufactured by this factory in the
past 30 days.
~
FC_RAW
Raw Material Stock
This shows the current stock of raw material in this factory.
Raw material stock capacity in a factory is 500.
Make sure that you set your finished goods production to match this raw material.
~
FC_PROD
Product Stock
This shows the current stock of finished goods in this factory.
Finished goods stock capacity in a factory is 500.
Make sure that there is a market linked to your factory so that these goods can be sold.
~
CANCELWP
Cancel weapon production
Click on this X to cancel production of the weapon that is currently being produced.
~
CANCELSHP
Cancel building this Ship
Click on this to cancel the production of the ship currently being built.
~
CANCELTRA
Cancel Training
Click on this to cancel the training of the unit.
~
WEAPNUM
Production amount
Click here until you see the number of this type of weapon that you wish to produce.
The maximum number that you can enter is 20.
To decrease the number, right-click on the button.
~
SLIDER
Workforce Level
Slide this marker left or right to decrease or increase the maximum size of the workforce that you wish to employ in the building.
~
CANCELBLD
Cancel construction
Clicking here will cancel the building of this structure.
~
MN_PROD
Monthly Production
This shows the quantity of the product manufactured by this factory in the past 30 days.
~
MN_STOCK
Mined Stock
This shows the amount of material that has already been mined and is being stored at the mine.
~
MN_UNTAP
Untapped Reserve
This shows the amount of the natural resource still remaining underground.
~
IMPORT
Yearly Import
This shows the monetary amount of your yearly imports from the selected Kingdom.
~
EXPORT
Yearly Export
This shows the monetary amount of your yearly exports to the selected Kingdom.
~
STATTIME
Duration of the Current Status
This shows the amount of time that you have been in the current diplomatic status with the selected Kingdom or Kwyzan.
~
PEACE
Continuous Peace
This shows the amount of time that you have been at peace with the selected Kingdom or Kwyzan.
~
ALLOWATK
Allow Attack
If this is set to "Yes", you will be able to target and attack the units and structures of the selected Kingdom or Kwyzan.
If it is set to "No", you will not.
~
AGGRESS2
Defensive Mode (Click or ALT-A to switch mode) 
When toggled to this mode your units will not fight unless attacked.
~
AGGRESS1 
Aggressive Mode (Click or ALT-A to switch mode) 
When toggled to this mode your units will automatically attack an enemy in their area, but will not follow it an unreasonable distance.
~
AGGRESS3
Stand Ground Mode (Click or ALT-A to switch mode) 
When toggled to this mode your units will not move for anything. If attacked they will fight from where they stand.
~
ASSASSIN
Assassinate
When you Click on this tile, your selected spy will attempt to assassinate the fort's King or General.
~
CAMPTOFORT
Upgrade Camp to Fort
Click on this icon to upgrade this building from a camp to a fort.
~
MIGRATE
Migrate
Right-Click on this icon to transfer one resident from the selected town into the town beneath this icon.
You will be unable to transfer a worker unless the targeted town is also linked to his place of work.
You will also be unable to transfer townspeople into a town of a different nationality.
~
WALLS-1
Build Town Walls
Click on this icon to begin construction of town walls.
Townspeople in a walled town can not be hurt in an attack.
~
WALLS-2
Upgrade Town Wall
Click on this icon to make your town walls higher and stronger.
~
BLESS
Unknown blessing
Click on this icon to receive an unknown blessing from your Greater Being.
~
GDINVOKE
Invoke Greater Being
Click on this icon to invoke the Greater Being.
It will then appear in the skies over the Seat of Power.
~
MAGIC
Use Greater Being Magic
Click on this icon and then left click on your target.
The Greater Being will then fly to the targeted area and use its magic.
~
TOWNLOCK
Town Lock
When this icon is green, linked forts or special structures will conscript their units from this town.
When this icon is red, the townspeople can not be conscripted.
Clicking on a red lock will open it (green) and allow the townspeople to be conscripted.
~
TOWNNAME
Town Name
This is the present name of your town.
You may change the town's name by Left-Clicking on the name in any single player ganes.
~
ROYAL-ON
Royal flag not raised
This shows that the unit is a "Common" unit.  Click on the R to designate him as a "Royal" unit.
Royal units may be carried over into the next game in the scenario.
You may designate no more than 10 Royal units.
~
ROYALOFF
Royal flag raised
This shows that the unit is a "Royal" unit and may be carried over into the next game in the scenario.
Click on the R to lower the flag and make the unit "Common".
~
FORTRS-1
Turn 4 Grokkens into a fortress
If you have four Grokkens selected, Click on this icon and then choose the site where you want the Grokkens to transform into a fortress.
~
FORTRS-2
Ungroup fortress
Click on this icon to ungroup your fortress into its four constituent Grokkens.
~
PATROL-B
Swarm Bheemas
Click here to swarm all the adult Bheemas from the Hyfe.
~
PATROL-T
Swarm Tarmes
Click here to swarm all the adult Tarmes from the Mownd.
~
TRAIN-B
Breed Bheemas
Click here to breed a Bheema.
This icon will be disabled if the Hyfe is full or if you do not have enough money or life points.
~
TRAIN-T
Breed Tarmes
Click here to breed a Tarmes.
This icon will be disabled if the Mownd is full or if you do not have enough money or life points.
~
STEAL_T
Steal Technology
Click on this icon to see a list of technologies that you can attempt to steal.
~
INCIDENT
Create an Incident
Click here to downgrade relations between the Kingdom or Kwyzan in which this spy is located and another Kingdom or Kwyzan.
~
RALLY
Set a rally point for units
Click here and then Right-Click on the main screen to set a rally point for all units produced in this building.  When completed the units will go to that point.
The rally point may be inside a fort, camp or town.
~
F_RALLY
Set a rally point for weapons
Click here and then Right-Click on the main screen to set a rally point for all weapons produced in this Vapngart.  When completed the weapons will go to that point.
~
RALLY-GO
View your rally point or set a new rally point
Click here to center your screen on your rally point.  You may then Right-Click on the main screen to change the present rally point.
~
RALLY-NO
Clear the Rally Point
Click here to clear the rally point that you have set for this building.
~
COLCODE
Color Code
Owner Identification
This colored diamond shows the color of this building's owner.
~
MAGIC1
Damage a Building
Click here and then on a building.  The building will then be damaged or destroyed. 
The Life Point cost will depend on the distance from the Tor.
~
MAGIC2
Freeze an Area
Click here and then on the screen.  All units under the square that you are allowed to attack will be frozen in place for 15 days.
The Life Point cost will depend on the distance from the Tor.
~
MAGIC3
Damage Units
Click here and then on the screen.  All units under the square that you are allowed to attack will be wounded or killed.
The Life Point cost will depend on the distance from the Tor.
~
MAGIC4
Teleport a Unit
Click here and then on one of your units.  Then click on the screen where you want your unit to be sent.
The Life Point cost will depend on the distance from the Tor.
~
MAGIC5
Cast a Magnified Light Attack
Click here to cast a magnified light attack in the surrounding area.  Nearby enemy units will be wounded.
~
MAGIC6
Bind a Greater Being
Click here to reach into the heavens and bind a Greater Being to your will.  Place the targeting square over your target and a Greater Being will be forced to attack for you.
~
MAGIC7
Cast a Freezing Wave
Click here to cast a wave of freezing plasma.  Any enemy units caught in the wave will be frozen for up to 15 days.
~
F_ENENGY
Progress of Construction and Level of Damage
These bricks and numbers show the progress of your building's construction as well as the level of damage that it has sustained.
~
T_ENENGY
Progress of Construction and Level of Damage
These bricks and numbers show the progress of your town wall's construction as well as the level of damage that it has sustained.
~
HITPOINT
Click to show all units' Hit Points (ALT-3)
Click this word to see the Hit Points of all units. 
~
LOYALTY
Click to show all units' Loyalty (ALT-1)
Loyalty shows the likelihood that a unit will betray you.  Units with 100 loyalty are the best.  Units with less than 30 may join your enemies.  The lower a unit's loyalty level, the more easy he is to bribe.
Loyalty can be increased with Honors or by serving under a strong leader.
~
LEADER
Click to show all units' Leadership (ALT-4)
Units with high Leadership skills should be cultivated as future commanders.  Never put a unit with high Leadership skills under the command of one with lesser skills.
A commander's Leadership skills will increase when he is given units to train, but it will increase the fastest when he leads troops in combat.
~
COMBAT
Click to show all units' Combat Skills (ALT-2)
Combat skill is slowly acquired when a unit is stationed in a Fort under a commander.  It will increase faster if the commander has high Leadership skills and if the unit engages in combat.  
Combat skills help to deterMine how powerful a unit is.  Most units will gain an additional combat technique when they reach a certain level.
~
UHPOINT
Hit Point
Hitpoints are the number of points of health that a unit possesses.  Once a unit's hitpoints reach 0 the unit will be killed or destroyed.
~
ULOYALTY
Loyalty
Loyalty shows the likelihood that a unit will betray you.  Units with 100 loyalty are the best.  Units with less than 30 may join your enemies.  The lower a unit's loyalty level, the more easy he is to bribe.
Loyalty can be increased with Honors or by serving under a strong leader.
~
ULEADER
Leadership
Units with high Leadership skills should be cultivated as future commanders.  Never put a unit with high Leadership skills under the command of one with lesser skills.
A commander's Leadership skills will increase when he is given units to train, but it will increase the fastest when he leads troops in combat.
~
UCOMBAT
Combat Skill
Combat skill is slowly acquired when a unit is stationed in a Fort under a commander.  It will increase faster if the commander has high Leadership skills and if the unit engages in combat.  
Combat skills help to deterMine how powerful a unit is.  Most units will gain an additional combat technique when they reach a certain level.
~
FORMTION
Set a Formation
Click here to order your troop into this formation.
Use your keyboard's number pad to set the direction that the formation is facing.
~
TPOP
This shows the Population of this Town
The maximum number of people that can live in a Town is 100.  Once you reach that level, no more people will be born.  It would be best for you to take several wagon loads of people out and settle a new Town.
~
TWORKER
This shows the number of Workers in your Town
Workers are those who work in Factories, Mines, Towers of Science, War Factories and Seats of Power.
Workers pay more taxes than Peasants and buy more goods from your Markets.  They are also more loyal.
~
TPEASANT
This shows the number of Peasants in your Town
Peasants are those who grow the food for your people.  If you have too many Workers and Soldiers and not enough Peasants you may very well run out of food!  When you build structures such as Mines and Factories near your Towns, Peasants will automatically go to work there, thus becoming Workers.
~
TLOYALTY
This shows the loyalty levels in this Town.
The present loyalty level is to the left and the future to the right.  In between you will see either a red or a yellow arrow.  The red arrow shows that the loyalty is falling while the yellow shows that it is rising.
If there is only one number, it means that the level of loyalty is stable.
~
TRESIST
This shows the resistance levels in this Town.
The present resistance level is to the left and the future to the right.  In between you will see either a red or a yellow arrow.  The red arrow shows that the resistance is falling while the yellow shows that it is rising.
If there is only one number, it means that the level of resistance is stable.
~
FIRMLOCK
Firm Lock
When this icon is opened, goods of the linked firms can be transfered freely between them.
When this icon is closed, goods can not be transfered between the linked firms.
Clicking on a closed lock will open it (circle) and allow the goods to be transfered freely between the linked firms.
~
WORKLOCK
Worker Lock
When this icon is opened, peasants of this town can work in the linked firm.
When this icon is closed, peasants of this town have no right to access the linked firm.
Clicking on a closed lock will open it (circle) and peasants of this town to work in the linked firm.
~
BUYLOCK
Buyer Lock
When this icon is opened, peasants of this town can purchase goods in the linked firm.
When this icon is closed, peasants of this town have no right to access the linked firm.
Clicking on a closed lock will open it (circle) and peasants of this town to purchase goods in the linked firm.
~
WORKER
Workers
This shows the number of job openings and the number of workers in the building.
These flesh colored icons show the number of workers in this building.  Green icons show jobs that have not yet been filled.  You may increase or decrease the amount of jobs on offer by sliding the slider (below) either left or right.
More workers means faster productivity.  Workers are also more loyal than peasants.
~
AUTO
Auto Production
Click on this word to set Auto Production in this Factory
Auto Production means that the Factory will produce finished goods with whatever raw material is available.  If one source of raw material is exhausted the Factory will switch production, assuming there is another raw material source linked to the Factory.
~
MANUAL
Manual Production
Click on this word to set Manual Production for this Factory (default)
Manual Production means that the Factory will produce only the finished goods that you have designated.
You may change the designation by Clicking on the Change Production Icon to the left.
~











